From f42bf32421ac930a426f87460a5143a949a65d76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:22:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] Keep Android's Up Next rows through a shuffle until the
 new order answers

When shuffle turned on or off, the upcoming tail closed its reads at once,
so the lane emptied until the new order's first read returned. The tail now
keeps the old order's reads and rows until the new order's count and first
rows arrive, as the Mac does. The test feed gives each count read its own
channel and can hold new reads, so a test can see the old rows stay.

