From 98110c8a3ca3dccf6722f761e5e3f9a82039ee55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:41:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] Hold a dragged volume until playback has stored it

Both apps cleared the dragged level when the stored volume changed, which
waits for a later query result and never clears when the drag ends on the
stored level. set_volume is now async: it answers once the progress fan-out
has written the level to the playback_now row, which it shows by forwarding
the level's VolumeChanged after the write. The Android slider and the Mac
slider hold the level the drag ended on until that call returns, then draw
the stored value.

